{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1439598-willpower-reduces-the-chance-for-a-botch","id":1439598,"title":"Willpower \"Reduces the Chance for a Botch\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-03-12T22:56:46-08:00","id":1439598,"title":"Willpower \"Reduces the Chance for a Botch\"","content":"Ok, something that drives me absolutely crazy in the Changeling the Dreaming 20th Edition Book is the inconsistencies with how willpower is used to affect rolls.<br /> <br /> Throughout the book it mentions that spending a point of willpower reduces the chance for a botch. Ex:&quot;A Willpower point purchases a single success on a dice roll. You may only spend one point per roll, but that guarantees a single automatic success (which also reduces the chance of a botch).&quot;<br /> <br /> A botch only occurs when a character rolls at least a single 1 and no successful dice.<br /> <br /> So, irrespective of how you treat the automatic success from willpower (either in the V20 method where ones do not cancel out the automatic success, or the C20 method where the rules kind of imply that they do) spending a point of willpower does not &quot;reduce&quot; the chance for a botch, it eliminates it completely. <br /> <br /> My thought is that whoever wrote the section on willpower didn't understand that botches only occur when there are zero successes and at least a single 1, and instead assumed botches occurred when there were more &quot;1&quot;s than successes.<br /> <br /> This even pops up again in the &quot;Because I Think I Can&quot; Merit. Anyone else run into this discrepancy or am I just misunderstanding some essential part of the rules. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26681-fazicar","name":"Fazicar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T13:26:57-07:00","id":1447727,"title":"","content":"I think you understand it perfectly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T14:15:55-07:00","id":1447731,"title":"","content":"You're just running into legacy language from older editions that wasn't completely scrubbed in the X20 books (it happens a lot).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T19:37:56-07:00","id":1451795,"title":"","content":"I think you're right, though that's how our game plays it... if you have more 1's than successes, you've botched. Spending a Willpower, in that case, actually does reduce the chance of a botch. I've seen it played both ways, guess you can pick which works best for your game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24663,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24663-observer","user":"Observer","date":". 06-11-2021, 10:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link"